        {
          "id": 1176045263,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "If you want it to show an escaped `\\n` as part of the string, then you need to change `len` here to `(next_offset - offset)` (or just have `proto_tree_add_item(tree, hf, tvb, offset, (next_offset - offset), ENC_UTF_8)`).\n\nIf instead you mean that you want the highlighted bytes to include the eol character but don't want the string value or the string displayed to include it, what you've done is what you want.",
